<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of the Pacific</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1879">1879</a>–<a href="/years/1884">1884</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Saltpetre War, Saltpeter War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of the Pacific was fought from 1879 to 1884 between Chile and an alliance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> over the nitrate-rich Atacama coast. Chile won at sea and on land and occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a> in 1881; it took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarapaca">Tarapacá</a> from Peru and the coastal province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antofagasta">Antofagasta</a> from Bolivia, which lost its access to the sea.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-the-pacific.jpg" alt="War of the Pacific" width="320" height="490" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: United States Federal Government · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:War_of_the_Pacific_LOC_map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
